course: dictionary
lesson: 12472
title: Deformation: a change of shape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deformation means a change in the shape of something. A force, which is a push or a pull, can cause it. «When Mia sat on the squashy cushion, it went flat.» The cushion has changed shape, so it has deformed, and deformation is the name for that change.
explain: Some changes go away and some do not. «The spring stretched when Sam pulled it, then sprang back to its usual shape when he let go.» That is elastic deformation. «The bent metal stayed bent after the crash.» That is plastic deformation, because the shape stayed changed.
explain: A deformation can also mean one part of something that has gone the wrong shape. «The dent in the car door is a deformation.» Here the word names the damaged part itself. Look for clue words such as shape, bent, squashed or stretched.
fact: Deformation means a change in the shape of something.
fact: A force can cause deformation: a push or a pull can bend, squash or stretch an object.
fact: «Elastic» deformation goes back to the original shape, like a spring.
fact: «Plastic» deformation stays changed, like bent metal.
fact: In geography, rocks can deform inside mountains and during earthquakes.
exercise: «The spring stretched when Sam pulled it.» What kind of change is this? | A sound | A change of colour | *Deformation | A hole
exercise: «The bent metal stayed bent after the crash.» Which kind of deformation is this? | Elastic deformation | Melting | *Plastic deformation | Cracking
exercise: Which word means a change in the shape of something? | Hibernation | Decoration | *Deformation | Illumination
test: «The plasticine ball was squashed flat by Ella's hand.» What has happened to the ball? | It has changed colour | *It has had a deformation | It has floated away | It has been eaten
test: After the earthquake, the rocks in the hills showed deformation. What does this tell us? | The rocks have grown smaller | The rocks have changed colour | *The shape of the rocks has changed | The rocks have turned into water
exam: «The spring went back to its usual shape, but the metal stayed bent.» The metal shows which kind of deformation? | *Plastic deformation | Elastic deformation | Chemical change | No deformation at all
